          "date": "2026-11-11 06:31:17.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20896 osc: fix unused variable in non-llcrypt build",
        "message": "LU-20896 osc: fix unused variable in non-llcrypt build\n\nWithout embedded llcrypt (CONFIG_LL_ENCRYPTION unset), the fallback\nosc_encrypt_pagecache_blocks() macro drops its inode, index and\ndirectio arguments, so a clang -Werror build of osc_brw_prep_request()\nfails with:\n\n  osc_request.c:1607:12: error: variable 'index' set but not used\n  [-Werror,-Wunused-but-set-variable]\n\nMake the fallback a static inline function with the same arguments\nas the llcrypt version, so the caller does not depend on which\narguments the implementation uses.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 659a80fa8361 (\"LU-20896 osc: encrypt direct IO pages at their own file index\")\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ifb221f12bc9f964d31f3bfd6bf31acc06a6a6964\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70246\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
